<title>NETHERLANDS: Heidemij reaches agreement on Articon acquisition.</title>
<headline>Heidemij reaches agreement on Articon acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch engineering consultancy Heidemij said on Monday it had reached an agreement for the takeover of BV Articon, one of Dutch Rail's (NS) two engineering firms.</p>
<p>In March Heidemij said it was in talks with Articon, which had turnover of over 55 million guilders in 1996.</p>
<p>No financial details were given on the deal.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
